Border widths snap as CSS snaps a border width: a width below one device pixel rounds up to one, a larger one rounds
down to whole device pixels (RmlUi rounded to nearest, which widened 1.5-pixel borders at fractional densities and
zooms).
CSS Values 4: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values-4/#snap-a-length-as-a-border-width

diff --git a/Source/Core/ComputeProperty.cpp b/Source/Core/ComputeProperty.cpp
index b1bce44..ff09b8e 100644
--- a/Source/Core/ComputeProperty.cpp
+++ b/Source/Core/ComputeProperty.cpp
@@ -276,7 +276,8 @@ uint16_t ComputeBorderWidth(float computed_length)
 	if (computed_length <= 1.f)
 		return 1;
 
-	return uint16_t(computed_length + 0.5f);
+	// Snapped as a border width: down to whole device pixels.
+	return uint16_t(computed_length);
 }
 
